    <h1>Ceratosaurus</h1>

    <hr>

    <h2>Overview & Time Period</h2>
    <p>The Ceratosaurus roamed during the Late Jurassic period, around 150 million years ago. Fossil evidence shows that it lived across regions that make up modern-day North America and Europe.</p>

    <h2>Distinct Physical Features</h2>
    <p>The Ceratosaurus was easily recognized by the prominent, blade-shaped horn sitting directly on its snout, along with smaller hornlets above its eyes and rows of small bony armor plates running down its back.</p>

    <h2>Hunting & Habitat</h2>
    <p>As a medium-sized terrestrial carnivore, it relied on powerful jaws, long blade-like teeth, and an agile build. It was an effective middle-tier predator that hunted various herbivores across ancient river floodplains.</p>

